# What the image must never contain.
#
# Render builds from the GitHub checkout, which already lacks all of this — but a
# `docker build` on the shop's own machine would sweep up everything in the
# working tree: customer repair tickets, bills, the accounts, 569 MB of
# photographs and the .env holding the OpenRouter key. Baked into an image, any
# of those would travel with every copy of it.

# Secrets.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# The shop's data. It lives on the mounted disk, never in the image. The two
# configuration files that ship with the code are let back in below.
nextjs/data/
!nextjs/data/backdrops.json
!nextjs/data/brands.json
runs/
*.xlsx
*.xls

# Rebuilt inside the image, and the wrong platform if copied from here.
**/node_modules
nextjs/.next
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.agent-cache

# Not needed to run.
.git
.github
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
nextjs/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
nextjs/.impeccable
